       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet because the dose looks wrong.\n\n**The problem:** Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to **6400 mg/day**.\n- The usual maximum for a single oral dose is **800 mg**.\n- The usual maximum for a full day of prescription dosing is **3200 mg**, given as 800 mg four times daily.\n\nThis order is twice the single-dose limit and twice the daily limit. That raises the risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury and cardiovascular events, even in a patient with normal kidney and liver function.\n\n**This may be a transcription error.** Did you mean one of these?\n- **400 mg four times daily** (1600 mg/day total). This is a common anti-inflammatory or pain regimen.\n- **800 mg four times daily** (3200 mg/day). This is the maximum.\n- Something else?\n\nTell me the dose you want and I'll enter it. If 1600 mg per dose is intentional, confirm it and give the clinical reason. I'll then enter it with a note saying the high dose was confirmed by the prescriber, though it may still need pharmacist review under your hospital's policy."
      }
