       "text": "I entered the order (ID **ORD-0001**): ibuprofen 1600 mg by mouth, four times daily.\n\n**Pharmacist review:** I added a high-dose alert to the order. It says the dose is twice the usual limits, that you confirmed it as written, and that no clinical reason was given. It asks for a pharmacist to verify it before it's dispensed, so pharmacy may contact you for the reason.\n\n**If you meant a lower dose**, such as 400 mg four times daily, please cancel or change this order right away. I can enter the new one for you.\n\n**Monitoring:** At 6400 mg/day, I'd suggest:\n- **Kidneys:** check creatinine and urine output.\n- **Stomach:** consider GI protection, such as a proton pump inhibitor, and watch for signs of bleeding.\n- **Heart:** check blood pressure.\n- **Other drugs:** avoid giving other NSAIDs at the same time, and be careful with anticoagulants."
